{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f4cbfc58a683894a66b028420969bb75a35fe4acda1bd3dce0024062c11b2041", "sample_idx": 2, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "\"To access the print version of the article, a link is provided. The rules for the Sudoku puzzle are explained, with a twist: the numbers in the cells contained within grey lines must add up to the figures in the corner. This variation on the classic game adds an extra layer of complexity and challenge for players. The standard rule of not repeating numbers within each shape formed by grey lines still applies, requiring careful planning and strategy to solve the puzzle.\"\n\n\n \nAddition to the traditional Sudoku rules, the numbers in the cells contained within grey lines have a special condition. They must add up to the figures in the corner, which are given as part of the puzzle. This means that players need to think not only about which numbers can fit in each cell, but also about how the numbers in each grey-lined shape combine to reach the target total. This requires a combination of logical reasoning and basic arithmetic skills.\n\n\n \nThe puzzle is presented as a challenge for readers, with the solution available in a future edition. Specifically, the completed puzzle can be found in next week's Observer Digital Edition. This gives players a chance to try to solve the puzzle on their own before checking their answers against the official solution. The puzzle is a fun and engaging way to exercise your brain and improve your problem-solving skills.\n\n\n \nThe rules of the puzzle are designed to be fair and consistent, with no hidden tricks or exceptions. The condition that no number can be repeated within each shape formed by grey lines is a key part of the puzzle, and helps to ensure that the solution is unique and can be found through logical reasoning. By following these rules and using your problem-solving skills, you should be able to make progress and eventually solve the puzzle.\n\n\n \nOverall, the puzzle is a entertaining and challenging activity that can be enjoyed by people of all ages and skill levels. Whether you are an experienced Sudoku player or just starting out, the puzzle is a great way to exercise your brain and have fun at the same time. With its unique twist on the traditional Sudoku rules, the puzzle offers a fresh and exciting challenge that is sure to appeal to anyone who enjoys puzzles and games. \"", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"To", "logprob": -0.4850621223449707}, {"token": " access", "logprob": -0.12741480767726898}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.011057410389184952}, {"token": " print", "logprob": -0.00908290408551693}, {"token": " version", "logprob": -0.00012337400403339416}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.006715467199683189}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.01423866767436266}, {"token": " article", "logprob": -0.35127031803131104}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.004663780797272921}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.05299333482980728}, {"token": " link", "logprob": -0.013598544523119926}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.0052368370816111565}, {"token": " provided", "logprob": -4.029192859889008e-05}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.6017539501190186}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -0.003302004188299179}, {"token": " rules", "logprob": -0.12229210883378983}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.01616385206580162}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.3918595612049103}, {"token": " Sudoku", "logprob": -0.0336722806096077}, {"token": " puzzle", "logprob": -0.0008933129138313234}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -0.0006063529872335494}, {"token": " explained", "logprob": -0.43327829241752625}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -1.2040065485052764e-05}, {"token": " with", "logprob": -0.02624587155878544}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.010510211810469627}, {"token": " twist", "logprob": -1.869645357131958}, {"token": ":", "logprob": -0.4411865174770355}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.6070938110351562}, {"token": " numbers", "lo